y interaction — all type-safe, all local, no code generation steps in your build.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/dynamic-stubbing#Drive-callback-based-APIs":{"type":"section","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Drive-callback-based-APIs","role":"pseudoSymbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed return values only go so far. Real dependencies "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"compute","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":": a calculator multiplies its operands, a sync engine mutates state, a network service delivers results through callbacks."}],"title":"Drive callback-based APIs","kind":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Drive-callback-based-APIs"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/mocking-your-first-protocol#Create-the-system-under-test":{"title":"Create the system under test","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial you’ll test a "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that depends on a "},{"code":"PricingService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without writing a mock class by hand. You’ll mark a protocol with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Mockable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", let the macro generate the mock, stub what its method returns, and verify that your code actually called it."}],"role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","type":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Create-the-system-under-test","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Create-the-system-under-test"},"01-1-3-generated-mock.swift":{"highlights":[],"type":"file","fileType":"","identifier":"01-1-3-generated-mock.swift","content":["\/\/ Generated by the @Mockable macro — you never write this yourself.","#if DEBUG","class MockPricingService: Mock, @unchecked Sendable, PricingService {","    func price(for item: ArgMatcher<String>) -> Interaction<S